30213	10714	30017	2	\N	next	\N	stop	\N	OPTIMIZE TABLE on InnoDB rebuilds the table as a new copy (similar to ALTER TABLE ENGINE=InnoDB) and requires roughly 2x the table's current size in free disk space. For large tables use ALTER TABLE ENGINE=InnoDB, ALGORITHM=INPLACE to avoid full copy. innodb_undo_log_truncate=ON requires innodb_undo_tablespaces >= 2 to function. TRUNCATE TABLE is the most effective pattern for staging tables as it is DDL and bypasses MVCC versioning entirely.; on_success note: Proceed to step 3; on_failure note: Investigate	2026-03-01 09:33:09.381992
