30215	10715	30019	1	\N	next	\N	stop	\N	INNODB_METRICS index_page_splits and leaf_page_splits counters are the primary signal for page split activity. A UUID v4 or RAND()-based primary key causes every insert to land at a random B-tree position, splitting full pages and leaving the old half partially empty. UUID v7 (time-ordered) or AUTO_INCREMENT eliminates this. data_free on a clustered index table reflects page-level fragmentation.; on_success note: Proceed to step 2; on_failure note: Investigate	2026-03-01 09:33:09.381992
30216	10715	30020	2	\N	next	\N	stop	\N	OPTIMIZE TABLE requires approximately 2x the table size in free disk space and takes an exclusive lock on the table during rebuild. Use ALTER TABLE with ALGORITHM=INPLACE for online rebuild on MySQL 8.0+. MERGE_THRESHOLD range is 1-50; default is 50 (merge when page is < 50% full). Setting it to 45 causes merging at 45% fill, reducing split frequency. Changing the primary key type on an existing production table is a high-risk schema change requiring careful migration planning and application code changes.; on_success note: Proceed to step 3; on_failure note: Investigate	2026-03-01 09:33:09.381992
