30218	10716	30022	1	\N	next	\N	stop	\N	InnoDB secondary indexes use a 'mark delete' approach: when a row is updated or deleted, the old index entry is marked but not immediately removed. Purge threads clean these up asynchronously. If purge lags, secondary indexes accumulate dead entries proportional to the history list length. bytes_per_row significantly above expected record size indicates dead entry bloat. Resolve purge lag first if history list length > 10,000 before rebuilding indexes.; on_success note: Proceed to step 2; on_failure note: Investigate	2026-03-01 09:33:09.381992
